# Problem
I have a custom LivingEntity subclass where I override all name-related methods to hide nametags:

```java
public class RandomEntity extends LivingEntity {

    @Override
    public boolean hasCustomName() {
        return false;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean isCustomNameVisible() {
        return false;
    }

    @Override
    public Text getCustomName() {
        return null;
    }

    @Override
    public Text getDisplayName() {
        return Text.empty();
    }

    @Override
    public boolean shouldRenderName() {
        return false; // (I explicitly forced this one to be false, but it didn't worked)
    }
}
```

However, the game still renders a blank nametag above the entity. This only happens for LivingEntity instances that are **not** MobEntities.


When looking into the GeoEntityRenderer.hasLabel() method, I found the following logic:
```java
@Override
	public boolean hasLabel(T animatable) {
		if (!(animatable instanceof LivingEntity))
			return super.hasLabel(animatable);

		double nameRenderCutoff = getNameRenderCutoffDistance(animatable);

		if (this.dispatcher.getSquaredDistanceToCamera(animatable) >= nameRenderCutoff * nameRenderCutoff)
			return false;

		if (animatable instanceof MobEntity && (!animatable.shouldRenderName() && (!animatable.hasCustomName() || animatable != this.dispatcher.targetedEntity)))
			return false;

		final MinecraftClient minecraft = MinecraftClient.getInstance();
		boolean visibleToClient = !animatable.isInvisibleTo(minecraft.player);
		AbstractTeam entityTeam = animatable.getScoreboardTeam();

		if (entityTeam == null)
			return MinecraftClient.isHudEnabled() && animatable != minecraft.getCameraEntity() && visibleToClient && !animatable.hasPassengers();

		AbstractTeam playerTeam = minecraft.player.getScoreboardTeam();

		return switch (entityTeam.getNameTagVisibilityRule()) {
			case ALWAYS -> visibleToClient;
			case NEVER -> false;
			case HIDE_FOR_OTHER_TEAMS -> playerTeam == null ? visibleToClient : entityTeam.isEqual(playerTeam) && (entityTeam.shouldShowFriendlyInvisibles() || visibleToClient);
			case HIDE_FOR_OWN_TEAM -> playerTeam == null ? visibleToClient : !entityTeam.isEqual(playerTeam) && visibleToClient;
		};
	}
```

While the code prevents MobEntities from rendering their nametag (based on shouldRenderName() and hasCustomName()), there is no equivalent check for LivingEntity instances that are **not** MobEntities.

So, when the entity is a LivingEntity, the rendering logic falls through to checks involving scoreboard teams and visibility, which cause a nametag to render even if shouldRenderName() returns false or isCustomNameVisible() is false.


# Steps to reproduce
- Create a custom entity extending LivingEntity but not MobEntity.
- Override shouldRenderName() and isCustomNameVisible() to return false.
- Spawn the entity and observe the empty nametag rendered above it.

# Expected behavior
Nametag should not be rendered if shouldRenderName() or isCustomNameVisible() return false regardless of whether the entity is a MobEntity or not.

# Actual behavior
Nametag renders for non-Mob LivingEntity even if those flags indicate it should not be visible.


# Version
- Geckolib : 4.7.7
- Fabric : 0.116.6+1.21.1
- Minecraft : 1.21.1
- Yarn : 1.21.1+build.3


