## My investigation

I looked for the all the references of `LivingEntity` in geckolib, and found line 143 in `GeoModel.java` suspicious:
When the input entity is not a `LivingEntity`, the  partial tick returned by `getFrameTime` is not used.

https://github.com/bernie-g/geckolib/blob/6aca0225c888ab7dd0c86f9520f832e23db27768/Forge/src/main/java/software/bernie/geckolib/model/GeoModel.java#L143

I do not understand why we do not use partial tick when the input is not a `LivingEntity`,
but after setting a breakpoint to set `currentFrameTime = currentTick + mc.getFrameTime()` regardless of the class of input animatable entity, the jittering disappears.

